<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Fort Laramie (1868)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Fort Laramie Treaty of 1868 · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-clouds-war">Red Cloud's War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Fort Laramie of 1868 was an agreement between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and bands of the Lakota, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yanktonai">Yanktonai</a> Dakota and Arapaho that ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-clouds-war">Red Cloud's War</a>. It set aside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-sioux-reservation">Great Sioux Reservation</a>, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-hills">Black Hills</a>, for the Lakota and closed the army forts on the Bozeman Trail. The seizure of the Black Hills after gold was found there broke the treaty, and in 1980 the US Supreme Court ruled that the land had been taken illegally.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-fort-laramie-1868.jpg" alt="Treaty of Fort Laramie (1868)" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author or not provided · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Photograph_of_General_William_T._Sherman_and_Commissioners_in_Council_with_Indian_Chiefs_at_Fort_Laramie,_Wyoming,_ca._1_-_NARA_-_531079.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
